umoja-desktop (2026.46.6) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Ask Umoja: a floating type-ahead card (the Copilot key or a tap of
    Alt) with apps, switches, Settings pages, sums and questions as you
    type; a command-line program that isn't installed is offered for
    install first, then run in a terminal titled with its command. The
    full model name shows in its footer. Clicking a notification brings
    its app to the front (needs Mir 2.28.0-4umoja15, no GNOME-style focus
    stealing prevention for xdg-activation). Window geometry, workspace
    and monitor are remembered across sessions like mutter, and session
    restore adds missing workspaces. Ships gnome-shell 51.0's icons,
    greeter too. Overview previews no longer re-capture the screen every
    10 seconds; cross-GPU copy buffers are pooled (Mir umoja14). A click
    outside Quick Settings or the date menu closes it; window drags end
    once no button is held; tray menus lose the bar's pill styling;
    notification quick replies split malformed reply lists into chips.
    The demo tour fast-forwards long waits and leads with Ask Umoja.

